446
00:46:22,520 --> 00:46:32,070
Now, in a moment, we're going to take one big step back, and in order to help us to do that, I wanted to take one moment very quickly to look at this from the big picture.

447
00:46:32,070 --> 00:46:41,990
So, some of our listeners are already aware of using a tool like Pytest to run a test suite, and maybe they've used other types of tools like linting tools.

448
00:46:41,990 --> 00:46:49,470
So, if you take a big step back, what would you say pyre fly fits into when it compares to linting and testing?

449
00:46:49,470 --> 00:46:59,270
And how should our listeners think about using type checkers and LSPs and test suites and linters in their overall big picture Python development process?

450
00:46:59,280 --> 00:47:06,030
So, I think Pyre Fly and type checkers in general, you know, fit in together with both runtime tests and linters.

451
00:47:06,030 --> 00:47:14,070
I feel like there's like a perception that like linters give like non-critical warnings that, you know, are like best practices and suggestions,

452
00:47:14,070 --> 00:47:20,070
whereas I think type checkers mostly flag things that could lead to runtime errors.

453
00:47:20,070 --> 00:47:25,990
And of course, compared to runtime testing, I think it's useful to have both type checking and tests.

454
00:47:25,990 --> 00:47:35,430
The main benefit of type checking in addition to tests is that you kind of you almost get like 100% coverage for free because the type checker reads all of your code.

455
00:47:35,430 --> 00:47:40,350
You don't have to write explicit test cases that cover every single branch.

456
00:47:40,350 --> 00:47:49,270
And in addition to the command line type checking, the way language servers fit into this is just if you want like a rich IDE experience,

457
00:47:49,270 --> 00:47:54,910
so like to let you like understand the code better, navigate your code faster, the language server helps.

458
00:47:54,910 --> 00:48:05,710
And like the reason why Pyre Fly does both is that, you know, the information needed to compute the all the type errors for a project is kind of like a subset of, you know, what the language server does.

459
00:48:05,710 --> 00:48:11,030
Like the language server can also in the IDE gives you all the errors for the project.

460
00:48:11,030 --> 00:48:14,630
So, if you turn that make it a command line, then you have a command line type checker.

461
00:48:14,630 --> 00:48:19,230
So, if you implement it as a language server first, you get both.

462
00:48:19,230 --> 00:48:31,390
And the language server can help both, you know, humans and AI now because you can have this like MCP server then the your AI agent can know that oh, Pyreflite provides these services.

